{"name":"First Impression","hex":"#f4e5e7","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"first impression","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The event when one person first encounters another person and forms a mental image of them.","The state of not having been previously raised within a particular jurisdiction."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/first_impression"}],"entries":[{"title":"Prima facie","blocks":[{"text":"Prima facie is a Latin expression meaning \"at first sight\", or \"based on first impression\". The literal translation would be \"at first face\" or \"at first appearance\", from the feminine forms of primus (\"first\") and facies (\"face\"), both in the ablative case. In modern, colloquial, and conversational English, a common translation would be \"on the face of it\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prima_facie","wikidata":"Q837138"},{"title":"First impression (psychology)","blocks":[{"text":"In psychology, a first impression is the event when one person first encounters another person and forms a mental image of that person. Impression accuracy varies depending on the observer and the target being observed. \nFirst impressions are based on a wide range of characteristics: age, race, culture, language, gender, physical appearance, accent, posture, voice, number of people present, economic status, and time allowed to process. The first impressions individuals give to others could greatly influence how they are treated and viewed in many contexts of everyday life."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_impression_(psychology)","wikidata":"Q5454174"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Example_photo_1_of_a_prima_facie_speed_limit_-_Rapid_River%2C_Michigan_%28United_States%29.jpg/500px-Example_photo_1_of_a_prima_facie_speed_limit_-_Rapid_River%2C_Michigan_%28United_States%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, ht